<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-1309] Parquet Java uses incorrect stats and dictionary filter properties</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-1309</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/SPARK-24251&quot; title=&quot;DataSourceV2: Add AppendData logical operation&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;SPARK-24251&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;SPARK-24251&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, we found that the changes to use HadoopReadOptions accidentally switched the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/blob/8bbc6cb95fd9b4b9e86c924ca1e40fd555ecac1d/parquet-hadoop/src/main/java/org/apache/parquet/HadoopReadOptions.java#L83&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;properties that enable stats and dictionary filters&lt;/a&gt;. Both are enabled by default so it is unlikely that anyone will need to turn them off and there is an easy work-around, but we should fix the properties for 1.10.1. This doesn&apos;t affect the 1.8.x or 1.9.x releases (Spark 2.3.x is on 1.8.x).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
